  "summary": "kimichat ships a bundled cryptocurrency miner behind a Kimi-branded lure",
  "details": "The PyPI package 'kimichat' impersonates Moonshot AI's Kimi chat product (pyproject description: 'Python package wrapper for the bundled kimichat runtime'; placeholder author metadata authors=[{name='User'}]). The tarball ships a ~32 MB ELF at src/kimichat/resources/kimichat that self-identifies as 'ForgeMiner/1.4.1', a Rust/CUDA cryptocurrency miner. The advertised console script 'kimichat-run' invokes start.sh, which sets a hardcoded attacker wallet (FORGE_WALLET=prl1p2jan4dvkdfkt5r3pra7z96axrxjyjcgat9w7ldetlcy9wffm569sc9ux2t) and mining pool (POOL=45.151.62.119:3361), then chmods and executes the bundled binary against the installer's GPU. Running the tool the package advertises hijacks the installer's compute/electricity and opens an outbound Stratum connection to a bare-IP pool controlled by the author, with no chat functionality present.",
